    "text": "For Freundlich adsorption isotherm, a plot of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>axis</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>axis</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;gives a straight line, the intercept and slope fo rthe line is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4771</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, respectively. The mass of gas, adsorbed per gram of adsorbent if the initial pressure is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>04</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math>&nbsp;is _____&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>.",
